Reading: note B dragged to within 4 px of the checklist's left edge snaps to it (x 1033) and shows a 1 px guide, hidden after release; Cmd+Z returns it to its start and shows "Undo: Move"; docking the photo outlines the zone for 1 s; Shift-drag selects note A and the table (two frames, "2 selected"); the count bar delete hides both and Cmd+Z restores them ("Undo: Delete"); the context menu opens at the pointer with five entries, arrows wrap, Enter on Delete deletes and Cmd+Z restores, Esc closes; the zone header trash appears on hover, deletes the zone keeping its items, and Cmd+Z restores it ("Undo: Delete zone"); German menu labels; no overflow at 390 px. Earlier runs found the count bar clipped outside the canvas (now clamped inside) and a test-only Enter without key text; both resolved.

